# Tracked text files check out with LF on every platform.
#
# Two things in this tree read tracked bytes back and compare them. `//go:embed`
# pulls the contract fixtures and the shipped skills into the binary at compile
# time, and the scripts under .github/scripts parse tracked files line by line.
# Under git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) those bytes gain CRLF on
# checkout, so a Windows build of a commit embeds different content than a Linux
# build of the same commit. That is not hypothetical: it is what
# TestEncodeTOONMatchesCapabilitiesFixture measured on #549's observation lane,
# where the embedded fixture arrived with CRLF and the encoder's output did not.
#
# This governs munsu's own checkout only. Tests that build a git repo inside
# t.TempDir() inherit the host's git config instead, and set core.autocrlf
# themselves -- see initTestRepo in internal/fleet.
#
# Nothing tracked here is binary (`git grep -I` reaches every non-empty file),
# so text=auto has nothing to misdetect.
* text=auto eol=lf
